Package: DISCO
Title: DISruption in COrrelations (DISCO)
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Farnaz", "Fouladi", email = "farnaz.fouladi@nih.gov",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements DISCO (DISruption in COrrelations), a method for
    quantifying feature-specific changes in correlation patterns between two
    groups. DISCO identifies features whose relationships with other features,
    including those from different data modalities, are disrupted in a group
    of interest relative to a reference group.
